refused: d236_on_built_in_types.cy:9:1, line 9 column 1
 9 | op + [$a: i32, $b: i32] -> i32:
   | ^^^^
 what: `op +` here is for `i32` and `i32`, which are built in
 why:  a struct or union can define an operator for itself, but an operator is never defined for, or changed on, built-in types (D236)
